        <!-- Article Body -->
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Capacitor banks are installed to correct power factor. In a harmonic-rich plant they do the opposite: bank capacitance and system inductance form a parallel resonant circuit that amplifies the very harmonics it should ignore. At a copper processing facility in Zhejiang, that mechanism tripped every capacitor bank on energization, dragged power factor to <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">0.61</strong>, and left <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">5th harmonic current at 254 A</strong>. This case study traces the measurement, the resonance diagnosis, and the active harmonic filter (AHF) + static var generator (SVG) architecture that restored the network.</p>
<h2 id="the-plant-and-the-3-transformer" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">The Plant and the #3 Transformer</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Zhejiang Jinjia Special-Shaped Copper Co., Ltd. (Changxing County, Huzhou) produces oxygen-free copper rods, busbars, and specialty copper products. Its lines run on induction furnaces and frequency converters — non-linear loads that inject harmonic currents continuously.</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">The <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">#3 1600 kVA transformer</strong> carried the symptoms:</p>
<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed"><li>Capacitor banks tripped or failed the moment they were energized.</li><li>Capacitors were repeatedly damaged by overcurrent and overheating.</li><li>Frequency converters struggled to start at high load.</li><li>Power factor fell to <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">0.61</strong>.</li><li>Harmonic distortion reached levels that threatened equipment life and site safety.</li></ul>
<h2 id="how-the-problem-was-quantified" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">How the Problem Was Quantified</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Baseline measurements at the transformer established the scale before any equipment was specified:</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6"><table class="w-full border-collapse"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50"><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Parameter</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Measured Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">THDv</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">up to <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">7.72%</strong></td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">THDi</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">up to <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">28.5%</strong></td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Dominant harmonics</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">5th, 11th, 13th</strong></td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Reactive power demand</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">781 kvar</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">The <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">3-1# feeder</strong> (left branch) was worse: THDi up to <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">31.77%</strong>, THDv up to <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">7.92%</strong>, again dominated by the 5th and 11th. The 5th harmonic current alone measured <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">254 A</strong>; the 11th peaked at <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">139 A</strong> — both well beyond IEEE and GB limits.</p>
<h2 id="root-cause-parallel-resonance" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Root Cause: Parallel Resonance</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">The harmonic spectrum pointed to VFDs and rectifiers as the source. The failure mechanism was subtler.</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">A capacitor bank presents capacitive reactance that falls with frequency. System inductance rises with frequency. At one frequency — the parallel resonant frequency — the two cancel and the impedance seen by harmonic currents spikes:</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">f_res = (1 / 2π) × √(L_system × C_bank)</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">When a harmonic current lands near f_res, the bank becomes a trap: harmonic current circulates between capacitor and inductance, the bank carries far more current than its rating, and dielectric temperature climbs until the unit fails. This is why the banks tripped on energization rather than degrading slowly — the resonance was excited the moment the contactor closed.</p>
<h2 id="what-resonant-banks-cost" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">What Resonant Banks Cost</h2>
<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed"><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Capacitor failure</strong> — overcurrent and overheating destroy units; replacement is recurring, not one-off.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Power factor collapse</strong> — with the banks offline, PF sat at <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">0.61</strong>, driving utility penalties.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">VFD startup unreliability</strong> — distorted voltage disturbs converter control and trips drives at high load.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Thermal stress on assets</strong> — harmonic losses accelerate transformer and cable aging.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Safety exposure</strong> — overheated neutrals and failed capacitor cans are a fire risk.</li></ul>
<h2 id="why-fixed-correction-falls-short" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Why Fixed Correction Falls Short</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Two conventional remedies were on the table. Neither fully solved the problem.</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Detuned reactors plus capacitors (7%)</strong> shift the resonant frequency below the 5th harmonic, which prevents 5th-order amplification. This is a valid retrofit — but it is fixed, tuned to an assumed spectrum, and does nothing for the 11th and 13th. It also cannot supply continuously variable reactive power as furnace load swings.</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Plain capacitor banks</strong> correct average power factor only. They cannot track a swinging load, cannot rebalance phases, and in a harmonic-rich network they are the resonance source.</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">What the plant needed was a source that adapts: harmonic cancellation in real time plus continuously variable reactive support, with no tuned elements to resonate.</p>
<h2 id="how-chitek-ahf-svg-fix-it" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">How CHITEK AHF + SVG Fix It</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">CHITEK specified a hybrid active compensation architecture sized to the measured spectrum and reactive demand of the #3 transformer.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6"><table class="w-full border-collapse"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50"><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Device</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Quantity</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">CHITEK SVG</strong> (100 kvar per unit)</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">8 units</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">Dynamic reactive compensation, 800 kvar total</td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">CHITEK AHF</strong> (150 A per unit)</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">3 units</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">Filtration of 2nd–50th odd harmonics</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">The <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">static var generator</strong> is a voltage-source converter that injects or absorbs reactive current continuously, from <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">+300 kvar to –800 kvar</strong>, holding PF near unity as the furnace load moves. The <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">active harmonic filter</strong> measures load current, extracts the harmonic component, and synthesizes a cancelling current:</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">i_c* = i_L − i_s(fundamental)</p>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Both respond in <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">&lt; 5 ms</strong>, so the correction tracks the load rather than lagging it. Because there is no tuned LC element, there is no resonant frequency to excite — the failure mode that destroyed the original banks is structurally removed. The AHF also carries <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">3× neutral capacity</strong> for triplen harmonic filtering.</p>
<h2 id="igbt-vs-sic" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">IGBT vs SiC</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Conventional LV AHF and SVG units use IGBTs capped near <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">150 °C</strong> and switching typically below <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">20 kHz</strong>. Migrating to SiC MOSFETs (<strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">200 °C</strong> junction, ~<strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">10×</strong> breakdown field, <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">2–3×</strong> switching frequency, ~<strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">50%</strong> lower switching loss) widens control bandwidth and shrinks the cabinet. Higher switching frequency pushes the ripple beyond the harmonics being cancelled and shortens the correction loop — the direction CHITEK's LV AHF + SVG platform is built on.</p>
<h2 id="results-after-commissioning" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Results After Commissioning</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Post-commissioning measurements confirmed the change across every parameter:</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6"><table class="w-full border-collapse"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50"><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Parameter</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">Before</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-text-dark border-b border-border-light">After</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Power factor</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">0.61</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">&gt; 0.95</strong></td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">THDv</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">7.72%</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">&lt; 3%</strong></td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">THDi</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">28.5%</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">&lt; 5%</strong></td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Capacitor operation</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">failed</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">stable and functional</td></tr><tr><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">VFD startup</strong></td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium">unreliable</td><td class="p-4 border-b border-border-light text-text-mid font-medium"><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">100% success</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">The existing capacitor banks can now be energized safely because the harmonic currents that excited resonance have been cancelled. Frequency converters start reliably at full load, and reduced thermal stress extends equipment life. The installation meets <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">GB/T 14549</strong> and <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">IEEE 519</strong>.</p>
<h2 id="engineering-deployment-checklist" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Engineering Deployment Checklist</h2>
<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed"><li>Measure THDv, THDi, and the individual harmonic spectrum at the PCC over a full duty cycle — the worst case, not the average.</li><li>Compute the parallel resonant frequency of every existing bank against system inductance before energizing anything.</li><li>Size the SVG for the reactive swing (here <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">781 kvar</strong> demand against <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">800 kvar</strong> installed capacity), not the average PF.</li><li>Size the AHF for the dominant harmonic currents (5th at <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">254 A</strong>, 11th at <strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">139 A</strong>) plus headroom for load growth.</li><li>Verify neutral capacity if triplen harmonics are present.</li><li>Re-measure after commissioning against IEEE 519 limits and confirm capacitor banks energize without trip.</li></ol>
<h2 id="typical-application-profiles" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Typical Application Profiles</h2>
<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed"><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Copper and steel processing</strong> — induction furnaces and VFDs; AHF + SVG stabilize a harmonic-rich bus and restore capacitor operation.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Plants with failed capacitor banks</strong> — repeated capacitor failure is a resonance symptom, not a capacitor quality problem; measure before replacing.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Facilities facing PF penalties with high THDi</strong> — fixed banks cannot correct PF in this regime; active compensation can.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-text-dark">Mixed nonlinear load sites</strong> — rectifiers, drives, and welders on one transformer; combined AHF + SVG handle both distortion and reactive swing.</li></ul>
<h2 id="bottom-line" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Bottom Line</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Capacitors cannot correct power factor in a harmonic-rich system — they amplify the problem and fail. A CHITEK AHF + SVG pair removes the harmonics that excite resonance and supplies clean reactive power continuously, so existing banks work as intended. What is your plant's THDi at the PCC — and have your capacitor banks ever tripped on energization?</p>
        </div>

